Good afternoon,

We are instructed to notify a fleet collision on behalf of our client Larkspur Landscaping & Grounds Management, LLC. Our reference is GRS/AUTO/2026/0114.

Broker reference: GRS/AUTO/2026/0114
Insured name: Larkspur Landscaping & Grounds Management, LLC
Date of loss: 14 March 2026
Loss location: Ballenger Creek Pike at Elmer Derr Road, Frederick, MD 21703
Cause: Collision - avoiding action, trailer jackknife
Estimated loss: USD 320,000

A passenger vehicle pulled out in front of our client's F-550 and trailer on
Saturday morning. The driver braked, the trailer jackknifed and the combination
left the road, sheared a utility pole and struck a commercial building.

Our client's driver has a fractured sternum and rib fractures and was admitted for
two nights - that will be a workers compensation matter on a separate file. The
other vehicle did not make contact and left before troopers arrived.

There is third-party building damage, a utility recovery claim from Potomac
Edison, and about 40 gallons of diesel and hydraulic fluid on the ground with MDE
notified. We are looking to the motor policy, and to whatever plant cover our
client holds for the Bobcat and the trencher.

Attached:

  * the completed loss notice
  * motor assessor's report
  * damage schedule

Please confirm which of our client's placements you are handling and assign an
adjuster and an equipment appraiser. The plant is accruing storage.

